  "gameplay_notes": {
    "pond_turtle_proxy_caution": "This is a Zoo Curator gameplay abstraction, not husbandry advice. EAZA European Pond Turtle guidelines warn against indiscriminate reptile mixing and note competition/disease risks. The broad proxy is therefore limited to selected non-predatory pond/river turtles and low-conflict mammals occupying different habitat layers.",
    "tropical_birds_final_pass": "Final Tropical Birds evidence pass. Added modern named-zoo mixed-exhibit records for hornbills/turacos, South American macaws/aracaris, and selected cross-category partners. Broad Goeldi's Monkey + parrot/Amazon compatibility is an explicit Zoo Curator gameplay proxy requested by the designer, grounded in a 2024 EAZA multi-zoo survey documenting Goeldi's Monkey with Green-cheeked Parakeet and Golden Conure; it is not a claim that every listed parrot species has been directly exhibited with Goeldi's Monkey.",
    "tropical_birds_caution": "No blanket toucan/aracari, turaco, or hornbill complete-group proxy was added. These taxa can show aggression/predation/territoriality in mixed aviaries, so only documented combinations or existing specifically approved proxies are used.",
    "new_level4_carnivora": "Added Common Kusimanse (Crossarchus obscurus) and Egyptian Mongoose (Herpestes ichneumon) as Level 4 Carnivora. Direct named-institution compatibility: Common Kusimanse + Blue-Eyed Black Lemur (Memphis Zoo), Common Kusimanse + Diana Monkey (Newquay Zoo). ZooRope also documents Common Kusimanse with Hystrix cristata and Atherurus africanus, but these are not mapped to Cape Porcupine (Hystrix africaeaustralis). Egyptian Mongoose + White-tailed Mongoose is documented at Samjung The Park (2016), but White-tailed Mongoose is not in the current Zoo Curator roster."
  },
